# The image Worker consumes the built OpenXML executable and package sources.
# Do not send the full slideclone skill tree (examples, local renders, or user
# artifacts) to Docker: the SDK stage needs only the OpenXmlDeckBuilder source.
**
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!packages/
!packages/**
!skills/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/OpenXmlDeckBuilder/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/OpenXmlDeckBuilder/**
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/rebuild-real-pptx-native.js
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/lib/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/lib/**
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/adapters/
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/adapters/pptx-openxml-dotnet.js
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/adapters/render-libreoffice.js
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/adapters/diff-pixel-png.js
!skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/scripts/libreoffice-benchmark.js
# `dotnet publish` runs inside the SDK stage. Local bin/ and obj/ outputs can
# contain platform-specific OCR/ONNX binaries totaling multiple GiB; they are
# neither reproducible image inputs nor safe to copy into the build context.
skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/OpenXmlDeckBuilder/bin/
skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/OpenXmlDeckBuilder/bin/**
skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/OpenXmlDeckBuilder/obj/
skills/pd-hifi-slideclone/dotnet/OpenXmlDeckBuilder/obj/**
